evices. If you end up with a difficulty, let's say you need to troubleshoot something, right? You can of course, the customer may be involved, they may have their own team for troubleshooting, they may escalate to you. So using RatKid, they can give your tech support team access to the devices they want and they can finely specify which devices the support person will have access to. And if the ticket gets escalated to the tack in the end, you can easily engage the tack, you can engage engineering regardless of the time zone, We may have people like developers in the United States, they do not work in the same time zone as the tech support in APJC, for instance. It is complicated. If you're given the name and the email address of the Cisco developer, it's just a matter of seconds for you or the customer to authorize this developer to come and connect overnight, connect the data they need, maybe work overnight with the tech engineer, but you don't have to be present. You can, you don't have to. And of course, if you want to see what we're doing, you know, we share our screen or we, and by the way, Racket will also keep a complete log of the entire activity conducted by each individual. So you will know exactly who did what or what device at which point in time. So you can actually review later what happened and if you have any questions, we will answer. So that's what Racket does. It's really like an accelerator, something that is a lot powerful than any other solution we have from VPN automation, remote connectivity, and definitely a lot faster than just Webex. It can be combined with Webex, but you're not dependent on Webex any longer. Next slide, please. So we're going to jump into a demo, and this is my last slide.

