    transfer is done now. I have the luxury of talking about something we call automated RCA, auto RCA. Now before I deep dive into what this is you know really the idea behind it comes from TAC engineers every year handling upwards of 2.3 million cases new cases that come in from our customers and on those cases we have lots of files lots of diagnostic data to imagine a TAC engineer having to analyze that data by going through each file looking for certain issues certain things that they know how to look for, just seems, well, insane. So many years ago, we started down a path of automation to develop signature systems and analytic systems that run on every single file that goes and gets attached to a TAC case. Those analytics, those signatures report back insights to our TAC engineers that help them solve cases faster. And we heard from our partner community that you want that same level of knowledge, that same tooling, that same capability that our tech engineers use thousands of times a day. And that's really what AutoRCA is. We're taking that traditional approach of manual diagnostic analysis, looking at each file one at a time and accelerating that through an automated ITSM workflow that allows you to upload a file to your ticketing system, have it smart bonded over to our case system, either on a dormant or escalated case, letting our analytics engines fire off and start looking for problems and insights in any type of TAC knowledge we can apply to that file. And then we take those insights

